auth-secret

# What the verification suites leave behind. They take an output directory as
# an argument and default to `.`, so a run started without one drops its
# screenshots wherever it was launched — the repository root when you use the
# npm script, packages/web when you call the script by hand. Both are covered.
# Ignored rather than forbidden: the screenshots are genuinely useful while you
# are looking at them, and worthless afterwards.
/*.png
/exported.csv
/shots/
/packages/web/*.png
/packages/web/exported.csv
# A run once received a URL where it expected an output directory, and made a
# folder literally called `http:`. Ignored so the same slip cannot commit one.
/http:/

